4.11. Medley approach
Improved analytical methods, and an increased number of studies, will allow for more accurate PSD analysis for various categories of consumables ingested, allowing for the GARMI to be updated. Until such time, the consideration of the three scenarios discretely projects a GARMI that somewhat accounts for the identified underestimations. A combination approach of the scenario resulted in a GARMI of 0.7 g/week (Table 9). Hence pending further availability of data, our preliminary estimates indicate that humans could potentially be ingesting between 0.1-5g of microplastics per week.

